---
type: statement
kind: theorem
---

<script>
  import Proof from '$lib/components/proof.svelte';
</script>

For each $\stateVar \in \stateSpace^\circ$, the family $(\Prb^\epsilon_\stateVar)_{\epsilon>0}$ satisfies a large deviation principle on $\pathSpace{[0,\infty)}{\stateSpace}$ with good rate function $\rf_\stateVar: \pathSpace{[0,\infty)}{\stateSpace} \rightarrow [0,\infty]$ as follows.
$$
  @tag(eq-rf-integral)
  \rf_\stateVar(\pathVar) = \left\{\begin{array}{ll}
    \displaystyle\int_0^\infty \ode^*\big(\dot\pathVar(t), \pathVar(t)\big) \rmd t & \pathVar \in \acpathSpace{[0,\infty)}{\stateSpace}, ~ \pathVar(0) = \stateVar \\
    \infty & \text{otherwise}
  \end{array}\right.
$$

<Proof>

[%full](/statements/ldp) gives us our large deviation principle with rate function $\rf_\stateVar$ as in [](tag:eq-rf).
Fix $\pathVar \in \pathSpace{[0,\infty)}{\stateSpace}$.
If $\pathVar(0) \neq \stateVar$, then we already have $\rf_\stateVar(\pathVar)=\infty$.
Otherwise, $\rf_\stateVar(\pathVar) = \rf_{\pathVar(0)}(\pathVar) = \rf(\pathVar)$, and so [%full](/statements/need-ac) tells us $\rf_\stateVar(\pathVar) = \infty$ if $\pathVar \not\in \acpathSpace{[0,\infty)}{\stateSpace}$.
If $\pathVar \in \acpathSpace{[0,\infty)}{\stateSpace}$, then Propositions [%label](/statements/rf-upper-bound) and [%label](/statements/rf-lower-bound) tell us that
$$
  \rf_\stateVar(\pathVar) = \int_0^\infty \ode^*\big( \dot\pathVar(t), \pathVar(t) \big) \rmd t.
$$
This concludes that $\rf$ can be written as in [](tag:eq-rf-integral).

</Proof>
